Torchlight: two public hooks on Entity for working out skinned poses before the
frame, on the game's worker threads (the crowd fight's "cull+animate" is mostly
OGRE evaluating skeletons one entity after another during render-queue fill).
`_cacheBoneMatricesForFrame` runs the private `cacheBoneMatrices`, which stamps
the bones with the frame about to be drawn, so the frame's own lazy call finds
them current and skips the work; `_isAnimationDirty` is updateAnimation's own
test, so entities OGRE would not re-pose are left alone. Header only, no
behaviour change for a caller that does not use them. Not __SWITCH__-guarded:
every target runs the pass.

